{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "list_id": "medicine-2026",
  "run": 1,
  "simulation_id": "sim-28",
  "member_id": "sandberg-rickard",
  "model": "gpt-5.6-terra",
  "reasoning_effort": "high",
  "prompt": "prompts/medicine_committee_terra_round2_v1.md",
  "preferred_configuration": {
    "prize_parts": [
      {
        "ballot_id": "B030",
        "laureates": [
          "Jens Juul Holst",
          "Svetlana Mojsov",
          "Daniel J. Drucker"
        ],
        "citation": "for discoveries of GLP-1 physiology that enabled transformative therapies for diabetes and obesity"
      }
    ]
  },
  "alternatives": [
    "B045",
    "B002"
  ],
  "statement": {
    "case_for": "My configuration is unchanged. B030 most persuasively connects a defined fundamental physiological system to a mature and exceptionally broad therapeutic transformation in diabetes and obesity. The citation deliberately recognizes discoveries of GLP-1 physiology and their demonstrated therapeutic enablement, rather than assigning the entire later pharmaceutical-development chain to three individuals. On that narrower and scientifically coherent basis, Holst, Mojsov, and Drucker remain the strongest allocation across the physiological, molecular, and translational foundations described in the record.",
    "case_against": "The unresolved weakness remains substantial: Lotte Bjerre Knudsen is among the credited contributors, and the supplied evidence cannot decisively apportion foundational physiology, mechanistic development, and drug-development credit. A three-person award cannot fully represent that larger chain. B045 also has mature, direct preventive value against infection-associated cancers and a potentially more compact attribution, making it the principal competing configuration.",
    "responses": [
      {
        "member_id": "wahren-herlenius-marie",
        "point": "Wahren-Herlenius argues that B045's virus-like-particle vaccines offer a mature, durable preventive intervention against HPV infection and related cancers, with a comparatively coherent attribution to Lowy, Frazer, and Schiller.",
        "response": "I agree that prevention of infection-associated cancer is an achievement of exceptional medical importance and that B045 is the closest alternative. Yet its own record requires separating the proposed trio's scientific contributions from later vaccine development, trials, and implementation. Applying the same standard, B030 remains ahead because a defined physiological discovery has produced broad, established therapeutic benefit across two prevalent chronic diseases; its citation can preserve an appropriate boundary by claiming therapeutic enablement rather than all subsequent drug development."
      },
      {
        "member_id": "linnarsson-sten",
        "point": "Linnarsson stresses that B030 is defensible only if framed as recognition of core GLP-1 physiology and mechanistic advance, rather than a complete account of modern incretin-medicine development.",
        "response": "I agree, and this distinction resolves why the configuration has not changed despite the attribution concern. The proposed citation is intentionally limited to discoveries of GLP-1 physiology that enabled therapies. That framing supports Holst, Mojsov, and Drucker as representatives of the specified scientific arc without implying that they alone encompass industrial development or excluding the importance of other contributors."
      },
      {
        "member_id": "perlmann-thomas",
        "point": "Perlmann describes B002 as a focused and persuasive translation of RNA-processing knowledge into treatment for spinal muscular atrophy, while noting less settled boundaries among mechanism, platform, and clinical development.",
        "response": "B002 remains a strong alternative because its mechanism-to-treatment link is unusually direct and its two-person allocation is attractive. I retain it below B030 because the supplied discussion leaves its broader maturity and the division of credit across platform and disease-specific work less fully resolved, whereas B030's biological and therapeutic consequences have been established over decades."
      }
    ],
    "uncertainties": [
      "Whether excluding Lotte Bjerre Knudsen is ultimately fair once her drug-development contribution is weighed against the award's deliberately limited focus on GLP-1 physiology.",
      "Whether the supplied evidence sufficiently distinguishes the individual contributions of Holst, Mojsov, and Drucker across discovery, mechanism, and therapeutic enablement.",
      "Whether B045's mature preventive impact should take precedence over B030's broader therapeutic impact under common criteria."
    ],
    "conflict_note": "No candidate-specific conflict is apparent from the supplied profile. The documented collaboration with Christopher Burge and shared institutional setting in single-cell genomics do not establish a connection to a shortlisted candidate."
  }
}
